ace","type":"trail","detail":"Medieval bridge towers guard the western tip of the island. The roof terrace on Vauban's river dam is free and looks straight back at them.","evidence":{"n_sources":5,"of":15,"urls":["https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Strasbourg","https://www.francethisway.com/places/strasbourg.php","https://evendo.com/locations/france/strasbourg"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Winstub food: tarte flambee and choucroute","type":"experience","detail":"Alsatian tables run to thin cream and bacon tarts, sauerkraut with pork, baeckeoffe stew, and dry white wine by the small jug.","evidence":{"n_sources":5,"of":15,"urls":["https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Strasbourg","https://www.francethisway.com/places/strasbourg.php","https://evendo.com/locations/france/strasbourg"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Ride the city bike network","type":"activity","detail":"Flat ground and long protected lanes make cycling the natural way around, including over the Rhine bridge into Germany.","season":[4,5,6,7,8,9,10],"evidence":{"n_sources":4,"of":15,"urls":["https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Strasbourg","https://www.ricksteves.com/europe/france/strasbourg","https://www.visit.alsace/en/"],"method":"web"},"sources":["web"]},{"name":"Marne-Rhine Canal","type":"activity","detail":"4 km away","sources":["commons","wikidata","wikipedia"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":3,"sources":["commons","wikidata","wikipedia"]}},{"name":"Neustadt","type":"activity","detail":"2 km away","sources":["commons","wikidata","wikipedia"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":3,"sources":["commons","wikidata","wikipedia"]}}],"nearby":{"trails":[{"layer":"trails","cc":"FR","id":"39724","name":"La ceinture verte autour de Strasbourg","km":1.3,"bearing":"N","lat":48.5852,"lon":7.75166,"tier":2,"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Parc_de_lOrangerie_%C3%A0_Strasbourg_en_d%C3%A9cembre_%289646314391%29.jpg/1280px-Parc_de_lOrangerie_%C3%A0_Strasbourg_